That progressed by the time she was 20 into full-blown heroin addiction.

498
00:39:39,140 --> 00:39:45,820
And throughout this process, from 13 to 20, her parents lovingly corrected her

499
00:39:45,820 --> 00:39:50,140
at the level at which the behavior necessitated.

500
00:39:50,140 --> 00:39:56,240
Until they got to a point, the hardest probably decision that they could ever make in their lives,

501
00:39:56,240 --> 00:39:58,940
where they had to say, you can no longer live in our home.

502
00:39:58,940 --> 00:40:03,920
They did not take delight in that decision,

503
00:40:04,060 --> 00:40:07,240
but they knew that that decision was enabling her and harming them.

504
00:40:07,240 --> 00:40:10,760
They did it through tears of sorrow and prayers of lament

505
00:40:10,760 --> 00:40:15,520
with the hopes that this drastic measure would ultimately lead to her healing and restoration.

506
00:40:15,520 --> 00:40:20,400
Spoiler alert, it did.

507
00:40:20,400 --> 00:40:23,480
She had a radical encounter with Jesus.

508
00:40:23,480 --> 00:40:26,920
We were there when she got baptized, and she is now pregnant with her second child,

509
00:40:26,920 --> 00:40:30,000
walking with the Lord, super thankful for that.

510
00:40:30,060 --> 00:40:31,580
But I share that story.

511
00:40:31,580 --> 00:40:33,440
Yeah, we can celebrate.

512
00:40:33,440 --> 00:40:35,960
We can celebrate restoration.

513
00:40:35,960 --> 00:40:41,520
I share that story because what we're going to look at here in Paul in 1 Corinthians chapter 5

514
00:40:41,520 --> 00:40:44,100
is something similar in the family of God.

515
00:40:44,100 --> 00:40:52,700
He says that as brothers and sisters in the church family make decisions that are contrary to the will of God,

516
00:40:52,760 --> 00:40:54,720
that are disobedient to God's commands,

517
00:40:54,720 --> 00:41:00,220
it's actually our job as a loving family to confront sin in the midst of the body of church.

518
00:41:01,640 --> 00:41:06,120
And he's going to say that there's a point at which that the rebellion,

519
00:41:06,120 --> 00:41:10,560
the decisions are so harmful both to the individual, to the church,

520
00:41:10,560 --> 00:41:13,540
and also to the world around us looking inside, right?

521
00:41:13,540 --> 00:41:16,360
We're supposed to be salt to the earth, the city on a hill.

522
00:41:16,360 --> 00:41:17,920
The world is looking in and saying,

523
00:41:18,080 --> 00:41:20,320
you guys are ignoring this sin.

524
00:41:20,320 --> 00:41:22,720
You guys are supposed to be different.

525
00:41:22,720 --> 00:41:26,540
And so there's a point at which where Paul says,

526
00:41:26,540 --> 00:41:29,620
okay, for the good of the individual, for the good of the church,

527
00:41:29,620 --> 00:41:31,480
for the good of the world,

528
00:41:31,480 --> 00:41:36,520
we ask individuals to leave the church through tears of sorrow and prayers of lament

529
00:41:36,520 --> 00:41:39,040
with the hope of restoration.

530
00:41:39,040 --> 00:41:41,780
Welcome to church again.

531
00:41:42,860 --> 00:41:49,340
And our passage today, it's one of the most referenced passage for something that the church has come to call church discipline.

532
00:41:49,340 --> 00:41:52,020
Anybody grew up in church, heard of church discipline?

533
00:41:52,020 --> 00:41:52,860
Raise your hand for me.

534
00:41:52,860 --> 00:41:56,100
Can I just say, we're really bad at naming stuff as Christians.

535
00:41:56,100 --> 00:41:58,780
That's just not a good name.

536
00:41:58,780 --> 00:42:00,160
Like, I don't like that name.

537
00:42:00,160 --> 00:42:01,940
I'd rather call it church restoration.

538
00:42:01,940 --> 00:42:07,380
Because again, the whole point, the whole process is all about the restoration of the individual,

539
00:42:07,380 --> 00:42:08,800
the restoration of the church.

540
00:42:08,800 --> 00:42:11,080
We just, we're bad at naming stuff.

541
00:42:11,080 --> 00:42:13,900
So the goal is always restoration.

542
00:42:13,900 --> 00:42:16,580
There are actually, as I was studying, I was actually shocked

543
00:42:16,580 --> 00:42:20,200
that there are actually more passages about this process in the New Testament

544
00:42:20,200 --> 00:42:22,060
than I was even super familiar with.

545
00:42:22,060 --> 00:42:24,280
It's talked about more often than you would think.

546
00:42:24,280 --> 00:42:29,420
And the second most famous passage comes from the teaching of Jesus himself in Matthew chapter 18,

547
00:42:29,420 --> 00:42:33,700
where he lays out very specific steps for how this process should go.

548
00:42:34,320 --> 00:42:42,060
It's intended to be a long and slow process that starts with someone close to you that you trust coming to you privately and saying,

549
00:42:42,060 --> 00:42:49,400
hey, I see this thing in your life that you're doing that seems to be contrary to the teachings of Jesus.

550
00:42:49,560 --> 00:42:52,740
Can you help me understand why you're doing this?

551
00:42:52,740 --> 00:42:55,800
And ideally, that's where the process ends, right?

552
00:42:55,800 --> 00:42:58,180
Ideally, a good Christian says, yeah, you're right.

553
00:42:58,180 --> 00:43:00,700
I am doing this thing and I shouldn't be doing this thing.

554
00:43:00,700 --> 00:43:02,820
And thank you for bringing it to my attention.

555
00:43:02,820 --> 00:43:05,320
Ideally, that's where it should end.

556
00:43:06,120 --> 00:43:12,900
But if it doesn't, the steps that Jesus lays out essentially are him turning the volume up on the correction.

557
00:43:12,900 --> 00:43:20,840
You bring two or three other trusted brothers and sisters who love this person with no delight in it

558
00:43:20,840 --> 00:43:23,100
and say, hey, you're doing this thing.

559
00:43:23,100 --> 00:43:25,760
It is clearly in opposition to the teachings of Jesus.

560
00:43:25,760 --> 00:43:31,960
You are clearly living in disobedience and sin, and it is going to cause harm to you and harm to us as a family.

561
00:43:32,280 --> 00:43:37,580
Please, repent and turn back to God, receive the grace and forgiveness of Jesus, walk in obedience.

562
00:43:37,580 --> 00:43:43,980
And eventually, as that process goes on, if the individual continues to be unrepentant and say,

563
00:43:43,980 --> 00:43:49,360
I can do whatever I want, leave me alone, that's where we have to take drastic measures,

564
00:43:49,360 --> 00:43:54,400
not that we delight in, but with the hope of restoration.

565
00:43:54,400 --> 00:43:57,120
And I share all of that before we even read the passage,

566
00:43:57,760 --> 00:44:03,060
because where we're at in the passage in 1 Corinthians 5 is at the very end of this process.

567
00:44:03,060 --> 00:44:08,460
And so some of Paul's language is going to sound very strong and even harsh,

568
00:44:08,460 --> 00:44:15,020
but we need to understand in the context that so many conversations should have happened before this conversation, right?

569
00:44:15,020 --> 00:44:18,600
This is the loudest the volume gets in the conversation.

570
00:44:18,600 --> 00:44:24,240
And so as we read Paul's language, I just want to make sure that we have that in the background of our minds.

571
00:44:26,180 --> 00:44:29,300
So I'm breaking down the passage into three sections.

572
00:44:29,300 --> 00:44:36,740
My outline for this morning so you can follow along ultimately is that Paul says we should do this thing called church restoration.

573
00:44:36,740 --> 00:44:41,800
We should do it for the good of the individual that is in rebellion, in sin.

574
00:44:41,800 --> 00:44:45,900
We should do it for the good of the church, local body of believers,

575
00:44:45,900 --> 00:44:48,920
and we should do it for the good of the world around us.

576
00:44:48,920 --> 00:44:50,180
That's going to be my outline.

577
00:44:50,740 --> 00:44:54,040
First, let's look at for the good of the individual, starting in verse 1.

578
00:44:54,700 --> 00:44:55,620
Paul says,

579
00:44:55,620 --> 00:45:01,160
I can hardly believe the report about the sexual immorality going on among you,

580
00:45:01,160 --> 00:45:03,600
something that even pagans do not do.

581
00:45:03,600 --> 00:45:09,040
I am told that a man in your church is living in sin with his stepmother.

582
00:45:09,040 --> 00:45:14,820
You are so proud of yourselves, but you should be mourning in sorrow and shame.

583
00:45:14,820 --> 00:45:17,060
You should have removed this man from your fellowship.

584
00:45:17,840 --> 00:45:20,820
Even though I am not with you in person, I am with you in spirit.

585
00:45:20,820 --> 00:45:27,340
And as though I were there, I have already passed judgment on this man in the name of the Lord Jesus.

586
00:45:27,340 --> 00:45:30,180
You must call a meeting of the church.

587
00:45:30,180 --> 00:45:31,680
I will be present with you in spirit.

588
00:45:31,680 --> 00:45:34,280
And so there will be power of the Lord Jesus.

589
00:45:34,280 --> 00:45:38,440
Then you must throw this man out and hand him over to Satan.

590
00:45:38,440 --> 00:45:41,280
And listen, this is where it's important that we focus on the whole point,

591
00:45:41,280 --> 00:45:47,860
so that his sinful nature will be destroyed and he himself will be saved on the day the Lord returns.

592
00:45:47,860 --> 00:45:52,580
So Paul ultimately says this process that should have been happening,

593
00:45:52,580 --> 00:45:57,220
it's interesting that his language is actually harsher on the church than it is on the individual.

594
00:45:57,220 --> 00:46:01,580
Because the church had ignored their responsibility to call out this sin.

595
00:46:01,580 --> 00:46:04,660
This man was living in sexual sin with his stepmother.

596
00:46:04,660 --> 00:46:08,140
This is a sin that's actually illegal in the Roman Empire.

597
00:46:08,440 --> 00:46:16,460
The consequence for a secular person doing this was to be banished to an island by themselves.

598
00:46:16,460 --> 00:46:17,600
And some of you are like,

599
00:46:17,600 --> 00:46:20,640
it doesn't sound like that bad of a punishment right about now.

600
00:46:20,640 --> 00:46:23,200
I wouldn't mind being on an island by myself right now.

601
00:46:23,200 --> 00:46:27,920
But this is such a heinous act that even the secular world wasn't doing it.

602
00:46:27,920 --> 00:46:29,740
And the church has totally ignored this.

603
00:46:29,740 --> 00:46:34,360
And so Paul is going pretty hard at the church and saying,

604
00:46:34,480 --> 00:46:38,380
you're actually not fulfilling your responsibility to love this individual

605
00:46:38,380 --> 00:46:41,940
and to hopefully protect him from the consequences of his action.

606
00:46:41,940 --> 00:46:45,980
It's important that we define what sin is at the beginning of this.

607
00:46:45,980 --> 00:46:49,040
It's a word that we don't like to talk about very much in the church.

608
00:46:49,040 --> 00:46:53,360
Sin is anything that is contrary to the will of God for our lives.

609
00:46:53,420 --> 00:46:54,840
And like I said in my prayer at the beginning,

610
00:46:54,840 --> 00:46:58,860
God doesn't give us rules because he's a domineering cosmic killjoy.

611
00:46:58,860 --> 00:47:01,060
All of God's rules are in place.

612
00:47:01,060 --> 00:47:03,080
Because when we disobey them,

613
00:47:03,080 --> 00:47:05,880
we will ultimately harm ourselves and others around us.

614
00:47:05,880 --> 00:47:09,540
God gives us rules to increase our joy.

615
00:47:09,540 --> 00:47:12,840
And the church should know that more than anybody else in the world.

616
00:47:12,840 --> 00:47:15,440
We are the ones whom he has given us the spirit that cries out,

617
00:47:15,440 --> 00:47:16,520
Abba, Father.

618
00:47:17,200 --> 00:47:22,680
We understand that he is a loving father who created us on purpose for a reason.

619
00:47:22,680 --> 00:47:27,320
And yet, instead of agreeing with the father's loving rule and reign,

620
00:47:27,320 --> 00:47:31,900
the Corinthian church chose to turn a blind eye to the sin of the individual and their family.

621
00:47:31,900 --> 00:47:36,620
And partly because they ignored it, it escalated.

622
00:47:36,620 --> 00:47:39,480
Sin escalates in our lives, right?

623
00:47:39,480 --> 00:47:42,480
No genuine follower of Jesus wakes up one day and says,

624
00:47:42,480 --> 00:47:43,280
you know what I'm going to do?

625
00:47:43,280 --> 00:47:45,760
I feel like having an affair with my stepmom.

626
00:47:45,760 --> 00:47:47,940
Right?

627
00:47:47,940 --> 00:47:50,760
Like, that doesn't happen immediately overnight.

628
00:47:50,760 --> 00:47:55,500
This is a sin that grows, that increases.

629
00:47:55,500 --> 00:48:00,960
However, when we take steps in a direction towards sin

630
00:48:00,960 --> 00:48:05,660
and our loving brothers and sisters see us going down a path that's destructive and we ignore it,

631
00:48:05,660 --> 00:48:13,340
partly on us to allow that pattern to continue to grow.

632
00:48:15,200 --> 00:48:17,580
In this particular case, like I said, it got so out of hand,

633
00:48:17,580 --> 00:48:20,780
not even non-Christians would have tolerated this kind of behavior.

634
00:48:20,780 --> 00:48:24,840
Paul says, you've ignored your responsibility to lovingly correct your brother,

635
00:48:24,840 --> 00:48:27,240
and it has spiraled totally out of control.

636
00:48:27,240 --> 00:48:30,060
And I don't think the Corinthians are alone in this.

637
00:48:30,060 --> 00:48:35,260
I think many of us, probably most of us, if I had to guess,

638
00:48:35,540 --> 00:48:39,700
are also eager to ignore sin in the lives of those around us.

639
00:48:39,700 --> 00:48:41,920
Why?

640
00:48:41,920 --> 00:48:42,940
Why do we do this?

641
00:48:42,940 --> 00:48:46,400
Why do we often choose to ignore these restoration conversations?

642
00:48:46,400 --> 00:48:54,180
Why do we often choose to not dive into this relational aspect where we're trying to call our brother and sister to obedience?

643
00:48:54,180 --> 00:48:59,180
If it really is, if we believe it, if we believe that sin causes damage to us and those around us,

644
00:48:59,180 --> 00:49:02,140
and we say we love our brothers and sisters that are around us,

645
00:49:02,140 --> 00:49:07,560
why do we refuse or ignore this opportunity to speak life into them,

646
00:49:07,560 --> 00:49:10,960
to invite them to repentance and to right relationship with God?

647
00:49:11,960 --> 00:49:14,900
A couple of guesses on my part.

648
00:49:14,900 --> 00:49:20,020
The first, I think we're often tempted to overemphasize our freedom in Christ.

649
00:49:20,020 --> 00:49:23,160
We say, yeah, they're sinning.

650
00:49:23,160 --> 00:49:24,820
We all sin.

651
00:49:24,820 --> 00:49:26,820
And Jesus forgives us, right?

652
00:49:26,820 --> 00:49:29,060
His forgiveness, His grace is unending.

653
00:49:29,060 --> 00:49:30,440
It's bounding.

654
00:49:30,440 --> 00:49:34,100
And so, really, at the end of the day, is it that big of a deal?

655
00:49:34,100 --> 00:49:35,640
We're all doing it.

656
00:49:35,640 --> 00:49:36,380
We all mess up.

657
00:49:36,380 --> 00:49:39,060
Why should I step in and say anything?

658
00:49:39,740 --> 00:49:43,300
Paul says in Romans 6 that when he preaches the gospel, right,

659
00:49:43,300 --> 00:49:47,780
he preaches the amazing, unending grace and forgiveness of Jesus,

660
00:49:47,780 --> 00:49:51,380
the temptation for us is to say, well, I'll just keep on sinning.

661
00:49:51,380 --> 00:49:54,480
So God's grace can keep on expanding and growing,

662
00:49:54,480 --> 00:49:58,540
and people can see that God forgives me even though I am totally in rebellion to Him.

663
00:49:58,540 --> 00:50:00,560
And Paul says, no, absolutely not.

664
00:50:00,560 --> 00:50:04,460
If you live that way, you have missed the point entirely

665
00:50:04,460 --> 00:50:07,320
because sin damages us and others.

666
00:50:08,340 --> 00:50:11,160
So we should be willing to enter into difficult conversations

667
00:50:11,160 --> 00:50:13,140
with our brothers and sisters when they are in sin.

668
00:50:13,140 --> 00:50:18,380
The second, we overemphasize the importance of an individual believer

669
00:50:18,380 --> 00:50:19,740
to the success of the church.

670
00:50:19,740 --> 00:50:26,020
We say, yeah, they're sinning, but they're really good at leading worship.

671
00:50:26,020 --> 00:50:29,500
They're a gifted preacher or teacher.

672
00:50:29,500 --> 00:50:31,160
They're such a faithful volunteer.

673
00:50:31,380 --> 00:50:33,520
They give so much money to the church.

674
00:50:33,520 --> 00:50:40,120
If we confront them in their sin, they'll leave, and that will damage the church.

675
00:50:41,980 --> 00:50:43,820
This is such an earthly perspective.

676
00:50:43,820 --> 00:50:46,560
Jesus will build His church.

677
00:50:46,560 --> 00:50:49,380
The gates of hell will not prevail against it,

678
00:50:49,380 --> 00:50:54,600
and no individual in the body is so important that sin should be ignored in their lives.

679
00:50:55,480 --> 00:51:00,180
And yet many stories have come out over the last 10 to 20 years in the American church

680
00:51:00,180 --> 00:51:05,700
where we have refused to address sinful patterns and behaviors in our leaders

681
00:51:05,700 --> 00:51:07,300
because we're afraid of the fallout.

682
00:51:07,300 --> 00:51:10,200
We're afraid of what people will think when it comes out,

683
00:51:10,200 --> 00:51:11,960
and so we hide it and we cover it up.

684
00:51:11,960 --> 00:51:16,120
And the reality is God is a good God, and He will not let sin go unpunished.

685
00:51:16,120 --> 00:51:17,920
It always comes out.

686
00:51:19,060 --> 00:51:24,040
And when the world sees that we're refusing to address it and hide it and cover it up,

687
00:51:24,040 --> 00:51:27,700
it actually leads to worse things.

688
00:51:27,700 --> 00:51:32,500
The best time to address sin is before it gets out of hand.

689
00:51:32,500 --> 00:51:37,020
The third thing I think we do is we overemphasize love of self.

690
00:51:37,020 --> 00:51:42,880
So we often justify not approaching someone for a hard conversation about sin in their lives

691
00:51:42,880 --> 00:51:45,300
because we say, well, I love them.

692
00:51:45,300 --> 00:51:46,360
I love our friendship.

693
00:51:46,840 --> 00:51:48,880
I don't want to get, I don't want to mess anything up.

694
00:51:48,880 --> 00:51:51,960
I don't want to hurt them.

695
00:51:51,960 --> 00:51:53,120
I don't want to hurt our relationship.

696
00:51:53,120 --> 00:51:56,140
And this is love of self disguised as love of others.

697
00:51:56,140 --> 00:52:03,340
We love our own comfort too much that we're unwilling to do something that makes us uncomfortable.

698
00:52:03,340 --> 00:52:06,640
And Paul says that it's actually for the good of our brother and sister

699
00:52:06,640 --> 00:52:10,840
that we should step into this really difficult thing for love of them.

700
00:52:10,840 --> 00:52:12,860
But we justify, we say, no, I don't want to do that.

701
00:52:12,860 --> 00:52:16,820
And actually, we're just loving ourselves more than we're loving our brother or sister.

702
00:52:16,840 --> 00:52:24,520
The individual that we are claiming to love is the one who will suffer the consequences when it spirals out of control.

703
00:52:26,120 --> 00:52:31,760
I've personally been in a situation before, multiple situations, but one that I remember fondly.

704
00:52:31,760 --> 00:52:37,340
And I literally almost talked myself out of having a conversation that I knew that needed to happen.

705
00:52:37,340 --> 00:52:37,820
Why?

706
00:52:37,820 --> 00:52:42,920
Because I was putting my own comfort in front of the genuine love for my brother or sister.

707
00:52:43,020 --> 00:52:46,480
I was saying, ah, this could be bad for our relationship.

708
00:52:46,480 --> 00:52:47,840
This could be bad for our friendship.

709
00:52:47,840 --> 00:52:48,820
This could hurt them.

710
00:52:48,820 --> 00:52:50,940
And at the end of the day, it wasn't about them.

711
00:52:50,940 --> 00:52:51,660
It was about me.

712
00:52:51,660 --> 00:52:58,020
So I think we often ignore this in our lives because we're way more concerned with our comfort

713
00:52:58,020 --> 00:53:01,040
than the flourishing of our brother and sister.

714
00:53:01,700 --> 00:53:06,920
And Paul is angry at the church for ignoring their responsibility to lovingly confront sin.

715
00:53:06,920 --> 00:53:12,240
Because at the end of the day, their brother is the one that is suffering the consequences.

716
00:53:14,160 --> 00:53:17,560
And now that it has been left unaddressed, it has escalated.

717
00:53:17,560 --> 00:53:20,480
And the only option is to remove him from the church.

718
00:53:20,480 --> 00:53:26,720
Again, tears of mourning, prayers of lament with the hope that he will ultimately be restored.

719
00:53:26,720 --> 00:53:33,960
Paul says, brothers and sisters in the church, it is our responsibility to confront sin lovingly

720
00:53:33,960 --> 00:53:38,120
and in relationship with one another so that the individual can be restored.

721
00:53:38,120 --> 00:53:39,740
It's all done for the good of the individual.

722
00:53:39,740 --> 00:53:43,520
Second, he's going to say it's done for the good of the church.

723
00:53:43,920 --> 00:53:48,460
Verse six, your boasting about this is terrible.

724
00:53:48,460 --> 00:53:54,320
Don't you realize that this sin is like a little yeast that spreads through a whole batch of dough?

725
00:53:54,320 --> 00:53:58,600
Get rid of the old yeast by removing the wicked person from among you.

726
00:53:58,600 --> 00:54:05,240
Then you will be like a fresh batch of dough made without yeast, which is what you really are.

727
00:54:05,240 --> 00:54:08,740
Christ, our Passover lamb, has been sacrificed for us.

728
00:54:08,740 --> 00:54:12,620
So let us celebrate the festival, not with the old bread of wickedness and evil,

729
00:54:12,720 --> 00:54:15,300
but with the new bread of sincerity and truth.

730
00:54:15,300 --> 00:54:20,760
The second thing Paul says is we have to address sin in the church for the good of the church,

731
00:54:20,760 --> 00:54:22,440
for the health of the church overall.

732
00:54:22,440 --> 00:54:27,800
And he uses a masterful illustration that has both practical and spiritual implications.

733
00:54:27,800 --> 00:54:32,680
And listen, it actually, it works both on an individual and a corporate level.

734
00:54:32,780 --> 00:54:37,620
This is like master class preaching here in verses six through eight.

735
00:54:37,620 --> 00:54:40,100
First, let's look at it on a practical level.

736
00:54:40,100 --> 00:54:42,960
Just as base level as we can.

737
00:54:42,960 --> 00:54:47,420
A small amount of yeast causes the entire batch of dough to rise.

738
00:54:47,420 --> 00:54:49,920
Do we got any sourdough people in here?

739
00:54:51,620 --> 00:54:52,480
Yeah, I love it.

740
00:54:52,480 --> 00:54:54,360
So I'll take a, what are they called?

741
00:54:54,360 --> 00:54:54,800
Feeders?

742
00:54:54,800 --> 00:54:55,820
I need one of those.

743
00:54:55,820 --> 00:54:56,820
Yeah, hit me up with that.

744
00:54:56,820 --> 00:54:57,060
All right.

745
00:54:57,060 --> 00:54:57,900
Right?

746
00:54:57,900 --> 00:54:59,120
A little bit of yeast.

747
00:54:59,120 --> 00:55:03,100
A very, very small amount of yeast spreads throughout the entire dough.

748
00:55:03,100 --> 00:55:07,820
And Paul says this is how sin works, both in the life of the individual and the life of the church.

749
00:55:07,820 --> 00:55:17,120
If you just allow a little bit, if you justify a little bit, if you theologize your sin away, if you explain it away, if you say, ah, well, it's not that big of a deal.

750
00:55:17,120 --> 00:55:18,320
I've got it under control.

751
00:55:18,320 --> 00:55:24,580
If we allow sin in our life unaddressed, it will spread.

752
00:55:24,580 --> 00:55:33,240
Again, like I said, no well-intended follower of Jesus wakes up one morning and decides to go off the ledge of sin.

753
00:55:33,340 --> 00:55:40,940
It starts much smaller and it escalates as we justify seemingly small amounts of inappropriate behavior that will grow and spread if left unchecked.

754
00:55:40,940 --> 00:55:41,800
A few examples.

755
00:55:41,800 --> 00:55:56,840
A little bit of gossip turns to slander, which gives way to bitterness and grows into full-out hatred that ruins relationships, causes damage inside and outside the church.

756
00:55:58,920 --> 00:56:07,200
Man, I think this is not in my notes, but I think that's what we're seeing nationwide on a political scale, right?

757
00:56:07,200 --> 00:56:09,900
We start with just a few jabs here and there.

758
00:56:09,900 --> 00:56:18,040
And all of a sudden, it spirals out of control until there's full-blown hatred of one another, picking up stones and throwing it.

759
00:56:18,080 --> 00:56:22,460
And we feel justified to do so because at stage one, we justified it.

760
00:56:22,460 --> 00:56:24,060
At stage two, we justified it.

761
00:56:24,060 --> 00:56:25,680
At stage three, we explained it away.

762
00:56:25,680 --> 00:56:31,800
And now all of a sudden, we're standing with these self-righteous attitudes saying, I can do this because it's actually for good things.

763
00:56:31,800 --> 00:56:32,360
You know what I mean?

764
00:56:32,360 --> 00:56:35,200
So like it just, a little bit of sin grows.

765
00:56:35,200 --> 00:56:40,140
A few envious thoughts leads to cutting corners at work, cheating, stealing, or a lack of generosity.

766
00:56:40,360 --> 00:56:45,280
Social drinking turns into every night of the week and it escalates into a full-blown addiction.

767
00:56:45,280 --> 00:56:53,220
A few lustful daydreams from a married individual gives way to regular pornography, which eventually gives way to a physical affair.

768
00:56:53,220 --> 00:56:54,960
And on and on we can go.

769
00:56:54,960 --> 00:56:56,100
We all know the stories.

770
00:56:56,100 --> 00:56:59,820
A little bit of sin spreads like yeast throughout the dough.

771
00:56:59,820 --> 00:57:01,080
You can't listen to me.

772
00:57:02,140 --> 00:57:03,620
I need to listen to myself.

773
00:57:03,620 --> 00:57:05,180
You cannot manage your sin.

774
00:57:05,180 --> 00:57:12,280
You have to kill it by the power of the spirit of God that lives inside of you.

775
00:57:12,280 --> 00:57:16,480
The same Jesus that rose from the dead has given you a spirit of power, not of fear.

776
00:57:16,480 --> 00:57:25,920
But if we ignore it, if we choose not to bring it to the Lord, we try and manage it ourselves, it will spiral out of control.

777
00:57:25,920 --> 00:57:27,120
Sin grows in the darkness.

778
00:57:27,120 --> 00:57:29,580
So we expose it to the light.

779
00:57:30,340 --> 00:57:36,600
And if we're not willing to expose it to the light, hopefully we have brothers and sisters around us who love us enough to say,

780
00:57:36,600 --> 00:57:42,080
I'm going to shine a little bit of light on this sin in your life that you're hiding because it's ultimately going to lead to your destruction.

781
00:57:42,080 --> 00:57:46,160
It's for the good of the church.

782
00:57:46,160 --> 00:57:53,440
Paul would later write that we are called to take every thought captive and make it obedient to Jesus.

783
00:57:53,440 --> 00:57:58,740
How often throughout the week are we filtering our thoughts through that idea?

784
00:58:00,340 --> 00:58:04,920
Yeah, okay.

785
00:58:04,920 --> 00:58:07,880
So then it also works on a corporate level, right?

786
00:58:07,880 --> 00:58:11,200
Individual sin spreads in our life as we ignore it and justify it.

787
00:58:11,200 --> 00:58:15,000
And sin also spreads throughout churches who are unwilling to address it.

788
00:58:15,000 --> 00:58:20,820
When churches refuse to address open, obvious, and unrepentant sin in its members,

789
00:58:21,060 --> 00:58:24,980
the rest of the members will get the message that sin is not that big of a deal.

790
00:58:24,980 --> 00:58:26,880
Right?

791
00:58:26,880 --> 00:58:33,480
Well, I'll just be like, ah, well, they're, you know, brother so-and-so is doing such and such,

792
00:58:33,480 --> 00:58:37,480
and the church doesn't seem to be concerned with it, so my sin must not be that big of a deal.

793
00:58:39,120 --> 00:58:45,940
And that is the worst thing that can happen to a church is if its members start to think that sin is not that big of a deal.

794
00:58:45,940 --> 00:58:52,200
My prayer is that our church will be full of individuals who take sin seriously in their own life

795
00:58:52,200 --> 00:58:56,840
and lovingly address sin in the lives of those who are in close proximity to them.

796
00:58:59,540 --> 00:59:06,820
Now, I feel the need to say this at this point in the message so that we don't, with zealousness, apply it inappropriately.

797
00:59:06,820 --> 00:59:14,200
The point of this message is not, I am not enlisting you as a private investigator of sin.

798
00:59:14,200 --> 00:59:15,460
Right?

799
00:59:15,460 --> 00:59:22,960
I am not asking you to start looking for every mistake that has been made by any individual in our church.

800
00:59:22,960 --> 00:59:27,220
This is why we love small groups here.

801
00:59:27,220 --> 00:59:32,720
This is why we encourage you to live in community, a small circle of brothers and sisters that you love and trust,

802
00:59:32,720 --> 00:59:37,620
because you're much more likely to receive correction from somebody who sits around your dinner table,

803
00:59:37,620 --> 00:59:40,660
who shares their own sin to you.

804
00:59:40,660 --> 00:59:43,980
You're much more willing to receive that correction.

805
00:59:43,980 --> 00:59:48,920
And so this process, it's meant to be done in community with people that you love and you trust,

806
00:59:48,920 --> 00:59:53,660
and it's not meant to be every single possible mistake anybody ever makes.

807
00:59:53,660 --> 00:59:53,940
Right?

808
00:59:53,940 --> 00:59:55,900
We're all broken, fallen, sinners.

809
00:59:55,900 --> 00:59:57,200
We make mistakes all the time.

810
00:59:58,160 --> 01:00:04,620
We're talking about things that are left unchecked, things that have potential to spiral out of control.

811
01:00:04,620 --> 01:00:10,840
He uses this illustration not just on a practical level, but on a spiritual level.

812
01:00:10,840 --> 01:00:16,240
And for those of us that have some background in the Bible, this will flow pretty quickly into this,

813
01:00:16,240 --> 01:00:19,680
but I'm going to do my best to explain it for those of you that are newer to the Bible,

814
01:00:19,680 --> 01:00:21,140
or at least newer to the Old Testament.

815
01:00:21,780 --> 01:00:26,000
If you're new to the Bible and you've kind of ignored the Old Testament for a while, I don't blame you.

816
01:00:26,000 --> 01:00:27,120
It is really good.

817
01:00:27,120 --> 01:00:28,800
You should work yourself into it.

818
01:00:28,800 --> 01:00:35,880
But for now, he talks about this yeast illustration really is rooted in the Passover celebration.

819
01:00:38,400 --> 01:00:43,560
And for those of you that don't know what Passover was, Israel was enslaved to Egypt for hundreds of years.

820
01:00:43,560 --> 01:00:47,240
God appointed Moses to free the Jewish people.

821
01:00:47,240 --> 01:00:50,300
He asked Pharaoh through Moses to let God's people go.

822
01:00:50,300 --> 01:00:51,380
Pharaoh refused.

823
01:00:52,340 --> 01:00:57,920
God sent multiple plagues throughout the entire nation trying to get Pharaoh's attention and say,

824
01:00:57,920 --> 01:01:03,500
look, I'm going to free my people eventually, so just relent and allow this to happen.

825
01:01:03,500 --> 01:01:05,680
And he continued to harden his heart and refused.

826
01:01:05,680 --> 01:01:11,320
And finally, the tenth and final plague, God warned that the firstborn son of every family would be killed.

827
01:01:13,400 --> 01:01:21,680
But if the Jews would obey God's law, sacrifice a firstborn spotless lamb and place its blood over the doorpost of their house,

828
01:01:21,680 --> 01:01:26,760
God would pass over their house and not allow that plague to fall on them.

829
01:01:26,760 --> 01:01:29,120
He would give them salvation from the plague.

830
01:01:29,120 --> 01:01:36,500
Knowing that Pharaoh would relent and let the people go, he told them to get dressed and ready for a long travel.

831
01:01:36,500 --> 01:01:41,720
And he told them to bake bread that didn't have yeast in it because they didn't have time for the bread to rise.

832
01:01:42,000 --> 01:01:43,200
It's unleavened bread.

833
01:01:43,200 --> 01:01:48,800
This happened just as God expected it to.

834
01:01:48,800 --> 01:01:57,560
And from then on, every year, the Jews were invited by God to celebrate Passover by ridding their entire house of any yeast for a week.

835
01:01:57,560 --> 01:02:07,400
The whole point of ridding their house of yeast was to remind them that God had delivered them from their slavery and death in Egypt.

836
01:02:09,700 --> 01:02:16,360
And Paul says, this Passover feast, this ridding our home of yeast has so much more significant meaning.

837
01:02:16,360 --> 01:02:19,560
Now look at verse 8, verse 7.

838
01:02:19,560 --> 01:02:23,960
Now that Christ, our Passover lamb, has been sacrificed.

839
01:02:23,960 --> 01:02:32,820
See, followers of Jesus, we believe that so many of the shadows of promises and covenants in the Old Testament are shadows of Jesus.

840
01:02:33,080 --> 01:02:35,120
None more clearly than the Passover.

841
01:02:35,120 --> 01:02:38,860
Jesus has replaced the sacrifice of Passover.

842
01:02:38,860 --> 01:02:41,700
He is the great Passover lamb.

843
01:02:41,700 --> 01:02:43,120
I love how John Mark Homer puts it.

844
01:02:43,120 --> 01:02:46,340
He says, Jesus is the climax of the Passover tradition.

845
01:02:46,340 --> 01:02:48,820
Jesus calls himself the lamb of God.

846
01:02:48,820 --> 01:02:49,860
He was the firstborn.

847
01:02:49,860 --> 01:02:51,540
He was without defect or sin.

848
01:02:51,540 --> 01:02:54,560
He was crucified on the same day as Passover.

849
01:02:54,720 --> 01:02:57,120
The timing gives the meaning.

850
01:02:57,120 --> 01:03:01,360
This is the stuff that gives me confidence in the gospel message.

851
01:03:01,360 --> 01:03:03,780
These things cannot be orchestrated.

852
01:03:03,780 --> 01:03:15,000
These circumstances that Jesus was crucified, they could not have been orchestrated to line up perfectly with the Passover festival from thousands of years ago.

853
01:03:15,140 --> 01:03:17,260
Jesus, he is our Passover lamb.

854
01:03:17,260 --> 01:03:24,260
And now, listen to this, instead of ridding our homes of yeast for a week to remind ourselves of God delivering us from slavery in Egypt,

855
01:03:24,260 --> 01:03:30,940
we are to daily rid our lives of sin, remembering that Jesus has set us free from slavery to sin and death.

856
01:03:30,940 --> 01:03:36,360
We no longer have to walk in slavery to sin, but we can walk in freedom through Jesus.

857
01:03:37,920 --> 01:03:46,820
We're called to take sin seriously in our lives for the good of ourselves, for the good of the individuals around us, and for the good of the church.

858
01:03:46,820 --> 01:03:57,520
And it starts with you and me searching our own lives, daily inviting the Holy Spirit to convict, to challenge, to encourage us to repentance, and to walk in holiness.

859
01:03:57,520 --> 01:04:04,060
Lastly, Paul's going to say that we do this for the good of the world.

860
01:04:04,560 --> 01:04:10,660
Verse 9, when I wrote to you before, I told you not to associate with people who indulge in sexual sin.

861
01:04:10,660 --> 01:04:12,740
So Paul's already written them a letter about this.

862
01:04:12,740 --> 01:04:14,200
They've had a conversation about it.

863
01:04:14,200 --> 01:04:20,260
And like churches often do, the Corinthians totally misunderstood and misapplied what Paul was saying.

864
01:04:20,260 --> 01:04:27,760
He says, I wasn't talking about unbelievers who indulge in sexual sin, or who are greedy, or who cheat people, or who worship idols.

865
01:04:27,760 --> 01:04:30,880
You'd have to leave the world to avoid people like that.

866
01:04:32,700 --> 01:04:42,840
I meant that you are not to associate with anyone who claims to be a believer, and yet indulges in sexual sin, or is greedy, or worships idols, or is abusive, or is a drunkard, or cheats people.

867
01:04:42,840 --> 01:04:45,680
Don't even eat with such people.

868
01:04:45,680 --> 01:04:56,060
It isn't my responsibility to judge those who are outside the church, but it is certainly your responsibility to judge those inside the church who are sinning.

869
01:04:56,560 --> 01:05:02,780
God will judge those outside the church, but the Scripture says you must remove the evil person from among you.

870
01:05:02,780 --> 01:05:10,840
See, Paul had written, he'd heard whiffs of this issue before, and he'd written to them and said, you gotta address this.

871
01:05:10,840 --> 01:05:13,340
And if they don't change, you can't associate with them.

872
01:05:13,340 --> 01:05:15,920
And the Corinthians are like, okay, so don't hang out with sinners.

873
01:05:15,920 --> 01:05:16,480
Got it.

874
01:05:16,480 --> 01:05:16,840
Perfect.

875
01:05:18,440 --> 01:05:21,120
Paul's like, no, that's not what I said.

876
01:05:21,120 --> 01:05:29,000
There are people outside of the church that are going to do all kinds of sinful things, and that is, your job is not to distance yourself from them.

877
01:05:29,000 --> 01:05:31,840
Your job is to love them with the message of Jesus.

878
01:05:31,840 --> 01:05:33,640
We talked about this a few weeks ago, missional living.

879
01:05:34,400 --> 01:05:38,800
But inside the church, that's where we are not to associate with people.

880
01:05:38,800 --> 01:05:46,000
And instead, the church got it backwards, and how often has the American church fallen prey to this exact same thing?

881
01:05:46,000 --> 01:05:49,340
How often are we so judgmental of those outside the church?

882
01:05:49,340 --> 01:05:58,120
How often do we paint up our picket signs and show up to protest non-Christian people not living according to Christian standards?

883
01:05:59,280 --> 01:06:01,360
Why would we ever expect them to do that?

884
01:06:01,360 --> 01:06:13,960
And meanwhile, those same people with the picket signs, protesting, and casting judgment on people who don't know Jesus are ignoring sin inside the church of people who do know Jesus.

885
01:06:13,960 --> 01:06:20,340
Isn't it crazy that the church 2,000 years ago did the same thing that we do today?

886
01:06:20,340 --> 01:06:23,680
The condition of the human heart, we're fallen.

887
01:06:23,680 --> 01:06:27,800
Paul says our job is not to cast judgment on people outside of the church.

888
01:06:28,460 --> 01:06:32,600
We can't expect those who are not submitted to the lordship of Jesus to be obedient to his teachings.

889
01:06:32,600 --> 01:06:33,520
That would be crazy.

890
01:06:33,520 --> 01:06:40,520
Our job is to welcome them around the table in love, listen to their stories, ask questions about their experiences,

891
01:06:40,520 --> 01:06:44,460
and look for opportunities to share with them the hope that we have found in Jesus.

892
01:06:44,460 --> 01:06:52,060
But for the church, as we read from the words of Jesus earlier,

893
01:06:52,060 --> 01:06:57,180
we, the church, are called to be salt to the earth, and what good is salt if it isn't salty anymore?

894
01:06:58,100 --> 01:07:02,720
What good is our lives to the world around us if our lives don't look any different?

895
01:07:02,720 --> 01:07:07,100
If we handle politics the same way the world handles politics,

896
01:07:07,100 --> 01:07:11,900
if we handle judgment and anger and hypocrisy the same way,

897
01:07:11,900 --> 01:07:19,280
what good is the message of Jesus setting people free from the bondage of slavery to sin if we live in slavery to sin?

898
01:07:20,420 --> 01:07:22,760
We are like salt with no flavor.

899
01:07:22,760 --> 01:07:32,960
We are like a light that hides ourselves under a bushel when we refuse to be in relationship with those who don't follow Jesus.

900
01:07:32,960 --> 01:07:38,540
If you don't hear anything else for the entire time, here's my main point.

901
01:07:38,540 --> 01:07:39,400
Write it down.

902
01:07:39,840 --> 01:07:45,220
God has saved you to change you, and he has changed you to have an impact on the world around you.

903
01:07:46,300 --> 01:07:54,120
God has saved you to change you, and he does that so you can have an impact on the world around you.

904
01:07:54,120 --> 01:07:57,580
And many of us are content to be saved without changing.

905
01:07:58,880 --> 01:08:05,840
Or we're saved, and we start to change, and yet we get to a point where we ignore our relationship with Jesus.

906
01:08:05,840 --> 01:08:08,540
We're just proud because we're pretty good at this whole Christian thing,

907
01:08:08,540 --> 01:08:11,760
and then all of a sudden we're separate out of relationship with God,

908
01:08:11,960 --> 01:08:18,400
and we start to justify and theologize and explain away why we're in total rebellion to his commands.

909
01:08:18,400 --> 01:08:23,760
When we choose to ignore our sin or sin in the church,

910
01:08:23,760 --> 01:08:28,360
we are rendering ourselves ineffective to do the very thing Jesus saved us to do.

911
01:08:28,360 --> 01:08:32,700
I'm by no means expecting perfection in the room.

912
01:08:32,700 --> 01:08:38,580
Jesus himself knows that I am far, far, far from that.

913
01:08:38,940 --> 01:08:44,720
But what he is expecting is intentionality and a willingness to address sin in our lives

914
01:08:44,720 --> 01:08:48,520
and to address sin in our brothers and sisters who we have close relationship with.

915
01:08:48,520 --> 01:08:50,380
Peter writes this,

916
01:08:50,380 --> 01:08:57,640
But just as he who called you is holy, so be holy in all you do.

917
01:08:57,640 --> 01:09:00,060
Jesus saved you to change you.

918
01:09:00,060 --> 01:09:03,460
He changed you to have an impact on the world.

919
01:09:03,460 --> 01:09:07,620
The reality is, I don't know about you,

920
01:09:07,660 --> 01:09:10,100
but the people that I talk to who are leaving the church,

921
01:09:10,100 --> 01:09:15,580
and I think the statistics in the American church would back this up,

922
01:09:15,580 --> 01:09:17,640
but the people that I talk to who are leaving the church,

923
01:09:17,640 --> 01:09:20,080
they're not leaving faith because of intellectual doubts.

924
01:09:20,080 --> 01:09:24,220
They're leaving faith because of the hypocrisy of the church.

925
01:09:24,220 --> 01:09:30,360
They're leaving faith because the church is way too focused on sin outside of the walls of the church

926
01:09:30,360 --> 01:09:35,400
and way too eager to ignore, justify, or theologize sin inside the church away.

927
01:09:35,400 --> 01:09:41,320
What the world around us needs more than ever is a unified group of followers of Jesus

928
01:09:41,320 --> 01:09:43,220
who take their own sin seriously

929
01:09:43,220 --> 01:09:49,160
and who have radical compassion and grace for those outside the church in sin.

930
01:09:49,540 --> 01:09:51,460
It's not that we ignore sin in their lives.

931
01:09:51,460 --> 01:09:55,540
It's just that we don't expect them to change apart from having an encounter with the risen Jesus.

932
01:09:55,540 --> 01:09:59,540
And this process of addressing sin in the church,

933
01:09:59,540 --> 01:10:05,840
it's been my experience that it rarely escalates to the point where you have to ask somebody to leave.

934
01:10:05,840 --> 01:10:06,660
Right?

935
01:10:06,720 --> 01:10:13,500
This is not something that we're eager to do or excited about doing or that happens often.

936
01:10:13,500 --> 01:10:20,360
But in rare cases, when someone who says they're submitted to the Lordship of Jesus refuses,

937
01:10:20,360 --> 01:10:25,560
refuses to acknowledge the warning of their brothers and sisters who are saying,

938
01:10:25,560 --> 01:10:28,140
you're headed down a road that's going to lead to your destruction.

939
01:10:29,620 --> 01:10:35,880
The most loving thing that we can do is through tears of sorrow and prayers of lament

940
01:10:35,880 --> 01:10:37,820
with the hope of restoration.

941
01:10:37,820 --> 01:10:40,480
Not let them off the hook.

942
01:10:40,480 --> 01:10:46,980
I've been a part of churches that take sin seriously for 10 plus years.

943
01:10:46,980 --> 01:10:49,660
I've seen this get to this point maybe twice.

944
01:10:49,660 --> 01:10:50,620
Maybe.

945
01:10:50,620 --> 01:10:55,320
This is not something that we get excited about or want to see often,

946
01:10:55,320 --> 01:10:57,400
but it's something that we have to talk about.

947
01:10:58,000 --> 01:10:59,880
I love how Warren Wiersbe puts it.

948
01:10:59,880 --> 01:11:01,020
He says,

949
01:11:01,020 --> 01:11:02,780
the very act of church discipline,

950
01:11:02,780 --> 01:11:06,580
let's call it restoration because we're bad at naming stuff.

951
01:11:06,580 --> 01:11:10,300
The very act of church restoration is a testimony to the world

952
01:11:10,300 --> 01:11:12,460
and a warning to the church,

953
01:11:12,460 --> 01:11:17,180
especially to new believers that God expects his children to be different from the world.

954
01:11:17,180 --> 01:11:22,840
To condone sin is to deny the very cross of Jesus.

955
01:11:25,340 --> 01:11:28,180
Jesus died for the forgiveness of our sins.

956
01:11:28,180 --> 01:11:31,280
And for us to ignore it like it doesn't matter or it's not a big deal

957
01:11:31,280 --> 01:11:33,480
is to deny the very cross of Jesus.

958
01:11:33,480 --> 01:11:37,920
So, as we begin to close,

959
01:11:37,920 --> 01:11:43,320
this was not a particularly fun message for me to write.

960
01:11:43,320 --> 01:11:46,940
Because me, like many in the American church,

961
01:11:46,940 --> 01:11:50,340
we love to focus on the incredible grace and forgiveness of Jesus

962
01:11:50,340 --> 01:11:54,860
while forgetting that he died to give us freedom from sin.

963
01:11:54,860 --> 01:12:00,860
We have to take sin seriously because God takes sin seriously.

964
01:12:00,860 --> 01:12:04,380
And God, listen to this,

965
01:12:04,380 --> 01:12:08,620
God takes sin seriously because it's harmful to you and to those around you.

966
01:12:09,620 --> 01:12:14,140
So, talking about sin is actually emphasizing God's incredible love for you.

967
01:12:14,140 --> 01:12:16,860
He created you in his image.

968
01:12:16,860 --> 01:12:20,520
He wants you to experience abundant life.

969
01:12:20,520 --> 01:12:25,140
And you can't do that when you're in slavery and bondage to sin.

970
01:12:25,140 --> 01:12:27,760
When you're trying to manage it all on your own.

971
01:12:27,760 --> 01:12:30,460
When you're trying to hide it in the dark and hope that it goes away.

972
01:12:34,460 --> 01:12:35,320
So, now what?

973
01:12:35,320 --> 01:12:38,960
Do we begin a chain reaction of conversations

974
01:12:38,960 --> 01:12:42,140
where all of us call each other out for every little mistake that we make?

975
01:12:42,140 --> 01:12:47,420
No, we do not.

976
01:12:47,420 --> 01:12:49,440
Here's what I would say.

977
01:12:49,440 --> 01:12:51,380
Believers, if you're in here, you're a follower of Christ,

978
01:12:51,380 --> 01:12:52,300
start with yourself.

979
01:12:52,300 --> 01:12:58,000
Daily, allow the Holy Spirit to examine your life.

980
01:12:58,000 --> 01:13:00,920
Give him the opportunity.

981
01:13:00,920 --> 01:13:03,480
Give him enough silence in the morning to speak to you

982
01:13:03,480 --> 01:13:05,080
and point out areas of your life

983
01:13:05,080 --> 01:13:08,560
where maybe just a little yeast has crept in

984
01:13:08,560 --> 01:13:11,020
and you've justified it or explained it away

985
01:13:11,020 --> 01:13:14,740
or come up with a theological argument

986
01:13:14,740 --> 01:13:16,440
for why it's not that big of a deal.

987
01:13:16,440 --> 01:13:21,340
Allow the Holy Spirit to speak truth to your life.

988
01:13:21,340 --> 01:13:23,860
Be willing to confess and repent

989
01:13:23,860 --> 01:13:26,700
and move forward in obedience.

990
01:13:26,700 --> 01:13:30,840
If you're going to have these conversations

991
01:13:30,840 --> 01:13:31,960
with brothers and sisters,

992
01:13:32,120 --> 01:13:33,580
do it in trusted relationships.

993
01:13:33,580 --> 01:13:36,320
Root it in prayer.

994
01:13:36,320 --> 01:13:38,700
Bathe it in prayer.

995
01:13:38,700 --> 01:13:42,700
And if you're going to go,

996
01:13:42,700 --> 01:13:44,820
make sure you've dealt with your own stuff first.

997
01:13:44,820 --> 01:13:45,580
Do it in love.

998
01:13:45,580 --> 01:13:46,460
Bathe it in prayer.

999
01:13:46,460 --> 01:13:49,320
And only escalate it when it is blatant,

1000
01:13:49,320 --> 01:13:50,200
unrepentant,

1001
01:13:50,200 --> 01:13:53,060
and multiple conversations have happened

1002
01:13:53,060 --> 01:13:55,120
with multiple people who love this person.

1003
01:13:55,200 --> 01:14:03,480
This is why it's good for the church, right?

1004
01:14:03,480 --> 01:14:05,820
If our church is filled with individuals

1005
01:14:05,820 --> 01:14:08,540
who daily allow the Lord to examine them

1006
01:14:08,540 --> 01:14:09,400
and point out sin,

1007
01:14:09,400 --> 01:14:12,480
our church will become holier.

1008
01:14:12,480 --> 01:14:15,960
Individuals in our church will become holier.

1009
01:14:15,960 --> 01:14:18,400
These conversations will need to happen less and less

1010
01:14:18,400 --> 01:14:20,760
because the Holy Spirit is doing the work

1011
01:14:20,760 --> 01:14:21,760
and our hearts first.

1012
01:14:21,760 --> 01:14:25,360
And even when we have to have the conversations,

1013
01:14:25,360 --> 01:14:26,720
our hearts will be prepped and ready

1014
01:14:26,720 --> 01:14:29,240
because the Holy Spirit's probably already been convicting us

1015
01:14:29,240 --> 01:14:31,600
of the sin that our brother comes to confront us in.

1016
01:14:35,220 --> 01:14:37,780
If you're in here and you are not a follower of Jesus,

1017
01:14:37,780 --> 01:14:39,380
you're new to faith or the church,

1018
01:14:39,380 --> 01:14:43,100
this might seem weird or harsh.

1019
01:14:43,100 --> 01:14:48,360
The reality is Jesus has called his church to be obedient

1020
01:14:48,360 --> 01:14:51,260
so that our message is consistent and compelling.

1021
01:14:51,260 --> 01:14:55,840
He's called us to be obedient for the sake of the world

1022
01:14:55,840 --> 01:14:57,040
outside of our walls.

1023
01:14:57,040 --> 01:14:58,800
And we haven't always done that well.

1024
01:14:58,800 --> 01:15:00,500
We haven't always done that well

1025
01:15:00,500 --> 01:15:03,000
because we don't often like to have conversations like this

1026
01:15:03,000 --> 01:15:03,960
inside of our walls.

1027
01:15:03,960 --> 01:15:06,920
So you got to experience a family conversation.

1028
01:15:06,920 --> 01:15:11,060
And ultimately, I would tell you that Jesus

1029
01:15:11,060 --> 01:15:12,980
is the fulfillment of the Jewish Passover.

1030
01:15:12,980 --> 01:15:16,780
He died and rose again to set you free

1031
01:15:16,780 --> 01:15:20,220
from slavery to sin and to give you an abundant life.

1032
01:15:20,220 --> 01:15:22,980
He says that my way is easy and my burden is light.

1033
01:15:22,980 --> 01:15:26,200
If you're in here and you've never trusted in Christ

1034
01:15:26,200 --> 01:15:28,620
for salvation, you've never allowed him to bring you back

1035
01:15:28,620 --> 01:15:30,200
into right relationship with the Father.

1036
01:15:30,200 --> 01:15:32,460
I'd love to talk to you more.

1037
01:15:32,860 --> 01:15:36,800
We've got volunteers that are at this very beautiful looking prayer tent.

1038
01:15:36,800 --> 01:15:39,840
Actually, if you go inside, it's really nice.

1039
01:15:39,840 --> 01:15:41,620
I know it looks a little bit sketchy from the outside,

1040
01:15:41,620 --> 01:15:45,660
but we'd love to have conversations with you about faith in Jesus.

1041
01:15:45,660 --> 01:15:51,780
If you're in here and you have been made aware of an area of sin

1042
01:15:51,780 --> 01:15:53,700
that's gotten a little too far down the road,

1043
01:15:54,080 --> 01:16:03,420
that you've been trying to find a trusted brother or sister in Christ.

1044
01:16:03,420 --> 01:16:07,860
Someone that you trust and confess to them what's going on.

1045
01:16:07,860 --> 01:16:10,860
Ask them for support and help and encouragement

1046
01:16:10,860 --> 01:16:14,520
because you know the destruction that is at the end of the road.

1047
01:16:17,000 --> 01:16:18,940
We're going to pray and then we'll take communion.

1048
01:16:18,940 --> 01:16:24,960
Father, we thank you again for this opportunity.

1049
01:16:24,960 --> 01:16:27,980
Just so reminded this week, God,

1050
01:16:27,980 --> 01:16:34,860
of my tendency to avoid thinking about talking about sin too much

1051
01:16:34,860 --> 01:16:40,260
and just such a reminder that you're a loving Father

1052
01:16:40,260 --> 01:16:44,160
who gives us commands because you love us.

1053
01:16:44,160 --> 01:16:51,740
God, just the beauty of being able to, for the first time, correct my son.

1054
01:16:53,180 --> 01:16:57,220
Knowing that I'm doing it out of love and I want him to flourish

1055
01:16:57,220 --> 01:17:03,180
and have peaceful and beautiful relationships with us and with those around him.

1056
01:17:03,180 --> 01:17:06,960
God, in such a, so much of a bigger scale,

1057
01:17:06,960 --> 01:17:10,340
that is why you give us your teachings, your commands.

1058
01:17:10,340 --> 01:17:13,240
That's what the Sermon of the Mount is all about.

1059
01:17:13,240 --> 01:17:17,840
Your invitation for your children to live in accordance with your will

1060
01:17:17,840 --> 01:17:20,160
that will lead us to abundant life and freedom.

1061
01:17:21,600 --> 01:17:24,540
God, may we not shy away from addressing the sin in our lives.

1062
01:17:24,540 --> 01:17:28,100
May we have open, soft, receptive hearts

1063
01:17:28,100 --> 01:17:30,100
when brothers and sisters come and confront us.

1064
01:17:30,100 --> 01:17:37,400
God, may your church become more holy,

1065
01:17:37,400 --> 01:17:41,020
more effective at missions to the world around us

1066
01:17:41,020 --> 01:17:43,840
because we take sin seriously.

1067
01:17:43,840 --> 01:17:46,780
It's in Jesus' name I pray.

1068
01:17:46,780 --> 01:17:47,860
Amen.

1069
01:17:47,860 --> 01:17:51,060
All right, we should have a map for you.

1070
01:17:51,600 --> 01:17:56,220
If you're new to Canvas, we take communion in an open way,

1071
01:17:56,220 --> 01:17:58,340
which means if you are a follower of Jesus,

1072
01:17:58,340 --> 01:18:00,640
if you have submitted your life to the Lordship of Jesus,

1073
01:18:00,640 --> 01:18:02,020
you're free to partake.

1074
01:18:02,020 --> 01:18:04,960
If you're not yet, if you haven't yet made that decision

1075
01:18:04,960 --> 01:18:06,800
or you're not sure if you've made that decision,

1076
01:18:06,800 --> 01:18:11,100
please just allow this time to be a time of prayerful meditation.

1077
01:18:13,100 --> 01:18:15,100
So, I'm going to dismiss.

1078
01:18:15,100 --> 01:18:17,740
We're going to follow the pattern on the map.

1079
01:18:17,740 --> 01:18:19,780
Get a wafer and a cup.

1080
01:18:19,780 --> 01:18:21,360
Come back to your seat.

1081
01:18:21,360 --> 01:18:24,360
And I will lead us in communion before we dismiss.

1082
01:18:24,360 --> 01:18:25,340
Go ahead.

1083
01:18:25,340 --> 01:18:27,340
Amen.

1084
01:18:55,340 --> 01:18:57,340
Amen.

1085
01:19:25,340 --> 01:19:27,340
Amen.

1086
01:20:55,340 --> 01:21:20,900
Once again in 1 Corinthians, if you ever want to feel good about yourself, read 1 Corinthians.

1087
01:21:20,900 --> 01:21:25,300
They're a bit of a mess, but so are we.

1088
01:21:25,340 --> 01:21:26,340
Amen.

1089
01:21:26,340 --> 01:21:27,340
Amen.

1090
01:21:27,340 --> 01:21:30,340
Paul talks to the Corinthians about communion.

1091
01:21:30,340 --> 01:21:33,340
And yet again, they had kind of missed the point.

1092
01:21:33,340 --> 01:21:36,340
Again, often like us.

1093
01:21:36,340 --> 01:21:43,340
Though the wealthy were gorging themselves on the body and blood of Christ to the point

1094
01:21:43,340 --> 01:21:44,340
where they were getting drunk.

1095
01:21:44,340 --> 01:21:51,340
And by the time the working class got to the service, there was no bread or juice left.

1096
01:21:51,340 --> 01:21:57,340
And the followers of Jesus that were there were incoherent.

1097
01:21:57,340 --> 01:22:02,340
So there are worse, you know, there are worse things.

1098
01:22:02,340 --> 01:22:04,340
Maybe we're not doing as bad as we thought.

1099
01:22:04,340 --> 01:22:05,340
All right.

1100
01:22:05,340 --> 01:22:14,340
But as he gives them some corrective instructions on communion, he asked them to use the Lord's

1101
01:22:14,340 --> 01:22:20,340
table, the body and blood of Christ as a regular rhythm for them to examine their lives.

1102
01:22:20,340 --> 01:22:24,340
Are they living in accordance with what God has commanded them to do?

1103
01:22:24,340 --> 01:22:30,340
Are there areas in their life or areas in the communion service where they are blatantly disobeying the whole point?

1104
01:22:30,340 --> 01:22:33,340
He says this in 1 Corinthians 11, 28 and 29.

1105
01:22:33,340 --> 01:22:39,340
That is why you should examine yourself before eating the bread and drinking the cup.

1106
01:22:39,340 --> 01:22:49,340
For if you eat the bread or drink the cup without honoring the body of Christ, you are eating and drinking God's judgment upon yourself.

1107
01:22:49,340 --> 01:23:09,340
So communion, it is an excellent regular rhythm for us as individuals to do the thing we talked about today, to allow the Lord to examine our hearts, to make us aware of areas in our life where we're in rebellion, areas of yeast that we are allowing in our lives.

1108
01:23:09,340 --> 01:23:17,340
Why this bread has no yeast in it, to remind us that Christ's body was perfect, spotless, holy.

1109
01:23:17,340 --> 01:23:20,340
He invites us to obey him.

1110
01:23:20,340 --> 01:23:38,340
So, as we take communion, I'd invite us to take a moment to examine our lives, think about sin in our life, confess sin to God or to a trusted friend.

1111
01:23:39,340 --> 01:23:46,340
So, I'm going to give you another 60 to 90 seconds to just examine yourself.

1112
01:23:46,340 --> 01:23:52,340
And before you take communion, feel free to confess sin to God prior to taking communion.

1113
01:23:52,340 --> 01:24:02,340
If you feel like you want to let this time pass and go to a friend after church and confess, that is more than acceptable, no judgment.

1114
01:24:02,340 --> 01:24:05,340
Let's take just a moment of silence now.

1115
01:24:05,340 --> 01:24:06,340
Let's take a moment of silence.

1116
01:24:06,340 --> 01:24:07,340
Let's take a moment of silence.

1117
01:24:07,340 --> 01:24:08,340
Let's take a moment of silence.

1118
01:24:54,340 --> 01:24:56,340
On the night he was betrayed,

1119
01:24:56,340 --> 01:24:59,340
celebrating Passover with his disciples,

1120
01:24:59,340 --> 01:25:01,340
he did a radical thing.

1121
01:25:01,340 --> 01:25:04,340
He took the bread and broke it.

1122
01:25:05,340 --> 01:25:08,340
He said, this is my body.

1123
01:25:08,340 --> 01:25:13,340
This is no longer about a one-year-old spotless lamb,

1124
01:25:13,340 --> 01:25:17,340
slavery from, freedom from slavery in Egypt.

1125
01:25:17,340 --> 01:25:19,340
This thing is about me.

1126
01:25:19,340 --> 01:25:22,340
I am Yahweh in the flesh.

1127
01:25:22,340 --> 01:25:25,340
When you take this from now on,

1128
01:25:25,340 --> 01:25:27,340
you do it in remembrance of me,

1129
01:25:27,340 --> 01:25:29,340
of what I am about to do,

1130
01:25:29,340 --> 01:25:31,340
what I am about to accomplish.

1131
01:25:31,340 --> 01:25:33,340
And so we, together today,

1132
01:25:33,340 --> 01:25:35,340
take the body of Christ broken for us.

1133
01:25:35,340 --> 01:25:46,340
We drink the blood of Christ shed for us.

1134
01:25:54,340 --> 01:25:56,340
Jesus, we love you so much.

1135
01:25:56,340 --> 01:26:02,340
So, so thankful today for your forgiveness and your grace.

1136
01:26:02,340 --> 01:26:04,340
There's no sin too far,

1137
01:26:04,340 --> 01:26:08,340
no path too far walked,

1138
01:26:08,340 --> 01:26:12,340
that we cannot turn back and expect you to be running to us,

1139
01:26:12,340 --> 01:26:15,340
to embrace us with your grace and your forgiveness.

1140
01:26:15,340 --> 01:26:19,340
God, may we take seriously sin in our lives,

1141
01:26:19,340 --> 01:26:22,340
because we know that you love us and that you want the best for us.

1142
01:26:22,340 --> 01:26:28,340
And may we be a more effective witness to a watching world,

1143
01:26:28,340 --> 01:26:31,340
because we're being conformed into your image.

1144
01:26:33,340 --> 01:26:34,340
We love you.

1145
01:26:34,340 --> 01:26:35,340
It's in Jesus name I pray.

1146
01:26:35,340 --> 01:26:36,340
Amen.

1147
01:26:36,340 --> 01:26:40,340
All right, church, go in peace.

1148
01:26:40,340 --> 01:26:42,340
There are a lot of good sporting events on today.

1149
01:26:42,340 --> 01:26:46,340
So if that is anything of interest to you, enjoy it.

1150
01:27:03,340 --> 01:27:04,340
Thank you.

1151
01:27:04,340 --> 01:27:06,340
Thank you.

1152
01:27:04,340 --> 01:27:05,340
Thank you.
